a few roles over the years

00:10:17.090 --> 00:10:18.690
that could've gone to either.

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:21.500
So Robert De Niro was considered

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:22.990
for the role of Michael Corleone.

00:10:22.990 --> 00:10:25.010
That role went to Al Pacino, forcing Al

00:10:25.010 --> 00:10:27.350
to bow out of "The Gang That
Couldn't Shoot Straight,"

00:10:27.350 --> 00:10:28.970
so Robert stepped into that role.

00:10:28.970 --> 00:10:30.830
Pacino was considered for "Taxi Driver,"

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:32.320
before De Niro landed the part.

00:10:32.320 --> 00:10:34.240
And Robert De Niro turned down the role

00:10:34.240 --> 00:10:37.880
of Coach D'Amato in "Any Given
Sunday," enter Al Pacino.

00:10:37.880 --> 00:10:39.290
You see kids?

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:42.910
In life, the inches we
need are all around us.

00:10:42.910 --> 00:10:45.493
- Because, that's what livin' is.

00:10:46.460 --> 00:10:48.260
- I'm goin' with Robert De Niro

00:10:48.260 --> 00:10:49.200
for the win.
(bell dinging)

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.033
Why?

00:10:50.033 --> 00:10:50.980
Because it's Wednesday,

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:52.860
and that's how I felt when
I woke up this morning.

00:10:52.860 --> 00:10:55.880
- This is such a crock of shit.

00:10:55.880 --> 00:10:57.370
- 'Cause figure it this way,

00:10:57.370 --> 00:10:58.600
better to be king for a night

00:10:58.600 --> 00:10:59.873
than a schmuck for a lifetime.

00:10:59.873 --> 00:11:03.200
(crowd cheering)

00:11:03.200 --> 00:11:04.430
- Could've gone either way,

00:11:04.430 --> 00:11:05.500
but it's not lost on me

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:07.470
that he is the lead in "The Irishman,"

00:11:07.470 --> 00:11:09.050
and he still carries a film

00:11:09.050 --> 00:11:11.170
in a way that few have
ever been able to do.

00:11:11.170 --> 00:11:13.380
He can also play comedies, multiple ways,

00:11:13.380 --> 00:11:16.810
and dare I say, his range
feels a little broader

00:11:16.810 --> 00:11:19.180
as we get towards our senior years.

00:11:19.180 --> 00:11:21.413
But that's just my opinion,
now it's your turn.

00:11:21.413 --> 00:11:23.240
Comment below and tell us

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:25.970
who the better all-time
great is in your peepers.

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:27.930
Is it Pacino, is it De Niro?

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:30.294
Or does Joe Pesci win,
in a write-in ballot?

00:11:30.294 --> 00:11:31.640
- Okay, okay, okay, okay, okay.

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.690
- Thanks for watching, I'm Mark Ellis,

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:35.250
and yes, I was talking to you.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:37.070
No one else here?

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:38.620
Must've been talking to you.

00:11:38.620 --> 00:11:40.270
It's a horrible Travis Bickle,

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:41.750
and that's how I'm walking out.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:43.370
Thanks, I'll practice.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:45.953
(upbeat music)

